" Remap Vim movement one key to the right:
"   j  k  l  '  =  left  down  up  right
"
" Original Vim:
"   h  j  k  l  =  left  down  up  right
"
" This file also preserves Vim's original single-quote mark jump on h.
" Example:
"   h a   behaves like old 'a
"   h h   behaves like old ''
"
" Put this in ~/.vimrc for Vim.
" For Neovim, put it in ~/.config/nvim/init.vim,
" or source it from your init.lua.

" -----------------------------
" Normal mode movement
" -----------------------------
nnoremap j h
nnoremap k j
nnoremap l k
nnoremap ' l

" Preserve original mark-line jump:
" old 'a  -> new h a
" old ''  -> new h h
nnoremap h '

" Optional: preserve exact-position mark jump too.
" old `a  -> new H a
" old ``  -> new H H
nnoremap H `

" -----------------------------
" Visual mode movement
" -----------------------------
vnoremap j h
vnoremap k j
vnoremap l k
vnoremap ' l

" -----------------------------
" Operator-pending mode movement
" -----------------------------
" This makes commands like d', y', c' work with your new right key.
" Example:
"   d'  = delete to the right
"   dj  = delete left
"   dk  = delete down
"   dl  = delete up
onoremap j h
onoremap k j
onoremap l k
onoremap ' l

" -----------------------------
" Optional: command-line mode
" -----------------------------
" Uncomment these if you also want the same keys while typing commands.
" cnoremap <C-j> <Left>
" cnoremap <C-k> <Down>
" cnoremap <C-l> <Up>
" cnoremap <C-'> <Right>
